  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Given that the minor of ${p}_{11}$ is $4$, find all the possible values of $t$ in the matrix\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}-5t & 18 & 6t \\\\ -3 & 9 & 5 \\\\ 19t & 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we remove the first row and first column:\n\n$$\nP=[\\begin{aligned}5t & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & 9 & 5 \\\\ \u2217 & 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe minor of ${p}_{11}$ is\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 3t\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =9\\cdot 3t-5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =27t-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${p}_{11}$ is $4$, so we must have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}27t-5 & =4 \\\\ 27t & =9 \\\\ t & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $t=\\frac{1}{3}.$",
